      "summaries": {
        "en": "Composio is an open-source TypeScript framework that simplifies building AI agents by providing unified access to 1000+ tools and APIs. Its technical innovation lies in abstracting tool discovery, authentication, and execution into a single interface, allowing developers to focus on agent logic rather than integration complexity. You can use it to quickly prototype agents that perform real-world tasks like data analysis or workflow automation, experimenting with different tool combinations in its sandboxed environment to test capabilities before deployment.",
        "zh": "Composio 是一个开源 TypeScript 框架，旨在简化 AI 智能体的开发流程，通过统一接口接入 1000 多种工具和 API，解决开发者集成多源工具的繁琐问题。其核心设计是将工具发现、身份验证和执行管理抽象为标准化层，让开发者能专注于智能体逻辑而非底层连接。你可以用它快速构建能执行实际任务的智能体，例如数据分析或自动化流程，在沙盒环境中测试不同工具组合，探索如何将自然语言指令转化为具体操作，从而加速实验和原型开发。",
        "es": "Composio is an open-source TypeScript framework that simplifies building AI agents by providing unified access to 1000+ tools and APIs. Its technical innovation lies in abstracting tool discovery, authentication, and execution into a single interface, allowing developers to focus on agent logic rather than integration complexity. You can use it to quickly prototype agents that perform real-world tasks like data analysis or workflow automation, experimenting with different tool combinations in its sandboxed environment to test capabilities before deployment.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "composio stands out for agentic-ai, agents, and ai in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Composio is an open-source TypeScript framework that simplifies building AI agents by providing unified access to 1000+ tools and APIs. Its technical innovation lies in abstracting tool discovery, authentication, and execution into a single interface, allowing developers to focus on agent logic rather than integration complexity. You can use it to quickly prototype agents that perform real-world tasks like data analysis or workflow automation, experimenting with different tool combinations in its sandboxed environment to test capabilities before deployment.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/ComposioHQ/composio for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
